# What NOT to send to the Docker build.
#
# Everything in this directory is uploaded to the build daemon before the first
# instruction runs. Without this file that includes target/ (20 MB of local
# build output) and uploads/ (66 MB of case-evidence photos) -- ~86 MB shipped
# on every deploy, to be immediately overwritten by the build or ignored.
#
# target/ is the important one for correctness, not just speed: COPY src ./src
# does not bring it in, but a stale local target/ in the context has caused
# enough confusion elsewhere that excluding it is worth the line.

target/
uploads/
.mvn/timing.properties

# Secrets must never enter an image layer. Nothing here should be committed
# anyway, but a build context is not a git checkout -- it is whatever is on
# disk, including files git ignores.
*.env
.env
*.p12
*.keystore
dev-keystore.p12

# Local noise
.DS_Store
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/
